{"id":"lobbied-before-the-vote","title":"Projects a lobbyist raised with a commissioner who then voted on them, 2022-2026","question":"After August 2022, how many projects decided by the commissions had been raised by a registered lobbyist with a commissioner who then voted, and how did they end?","finding":"Of 683 decisions at a street address, 85 came within a year after a lobbyist reported contacting a commissioner who voted on it about that address. Those commissioners cast 293 votes on them and 280 were yes votes. The lobbied projects were changed or disapproved in 23.5% of decisions, against 13.9% for the rest.","how":"The Ethics Commission's lobbyist contact file (contacts with City Planning officials, which include the commissioners, from August 2021) is searched for the street number and street name of each decided item; a contact counts when it is dated 0 to 365 days before the hearing and the official contacted is, by surname, among those whose votes are printed for the item.","limits":"Telling a commissioner about a project is permitted and reported, which is how it can be seen; contacts are often a request for a meeting, and outcome sought is usually approval. A surname match can join a contact with a staff member who shares a commissioner's surname. Lobbied projects are larger and more contested, so a higher rate of changes is expected. Clients who are people are not named. An address written differently in the lobbyist's report (a project name instead of a number) is missed.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"date","t":"Hearing","type":"date"},{"k":"case","t":"Case","type":"text"},{"k":"site","t":"Site","type":"text"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind of approval","type":"text"},{"k":"outcome","t":"Outcome","type":"text"},{"k":"contacts","t":"Contacts with voters in the year before","type":"int"},{"k":"officials","t":"Commissioners contacted (surname)","type":"text"},{"k":"votedYes","t":"Of whom voted yes","type":"int"},{"k":"clients","t":"Client (organizations only)","type":"text"},{"k":"lobbyists","t":"Lobbyist","type":"text"},{"k":"firstContact","t":"First contact","type":"date"},{"k":"daysBefore","t":"Days from last contact to hearing","type":"days"},{"k":"link","t":"Source","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"date":"2025-10-02","case":"2024-002799CUA","site":"906 BROADWAY","kind":"Conditional use","outcome":"Approved with changes","contacts":19,"officials":"Braun, Campbell, Imperial, Mcgarry, Moore, So, Williams","votedYes":7,"clients":"906 WORLD, 908 BROADWAY LLC","lobbyists":"Taylor Jordan","firstContact":"2025-07-28","daysBefore":3,"link":{"t":"Minutes","u":"https://sfplanning.org/cpc-hearing-archives"}},{"date":"2025-09-11","case":"2019-017622DNX","site":"570 MARKET STREET","kind":"Large-project approval","outcome":"Approved with the usual conditions","contacts":15,"officials":"Braun, Campbell, Imperial, Mcgarry, Moore, So, Williams","votedYes":7,"clients":"Frontier Group LLC","lobbyists":"Melinda Sarjapur","firstContact":"2025-04-23","daysBefore":8,"link":{"t":"Minutes","u":"https://sfplanning.org/cpc-hearing-archives"}},{"date":"2025-09-11","case":"2019-017622CUA","site":"570 MARKET STREET","kind":"Conditional use","outcome":"Approved with changes","contacts":15,"officials":"Braun, Campbell, Imperial, Mcgarry, Moore, So, Williams","votedYes":7,"clients":"Frontier Group LLC","lobbyists":"Melinda Sarjapur","firstContact":"2025-04-23","daysBefore":8,"link":{"t":"Minutes","u":"https://sfplanning.org/cpc-hearing-archives"}},{"date":"2025-03-27","case":"2025-000545OFA","site":"600 TOWNSEND STREET","kind":"Large-project approval","outcome":"Approved with changes","contacts":12,"officials":"Braun, Campbell, Imperial, Moore, So, Williams","votedYes":6,"clients":"Toda America, Inc.","lobbyists":"Denise LaPointe","firstContact":"2025-03-21","daysBefore":0,"link":{"t":"Minutes","u":"https://sfplanning.org/cpc-hearing-archives"}},{"date":"2025-02-13","case":"2023-011398CUA","site":"1111 PENNSYLVANIA AVENUE","kind":"Conditional use","ou